# The build is byte-reproducible, and that is load-bearing: `build.json` states
# a SHA-256, the cluster's mirror refuses an artifact that does not match it, and
# story-engine-v2 pins the same digest in `story-player.lock.json`.
#
# Line endings are therefore part of the contract. Git stores LF, but a checkout
# on Windows with the default `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into the working
# tree — and the bundler copies those bytes straight through, so the same commit
# builds ~1.5 KB larger with a completely different digest. Someone verifying a
# release from a Windows machine would conclude the artifact had been tampered
# with, when the only difference was their checkout.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to what CI has, so the digest is reproducible on
# every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by the text filter.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
